    "updated_at": "2022-01-19T15:15:28Z",
    "body": "> It seems there's some initialization internal to starship that gets counted as part of the first module evaluated, which can be misleading.\r\n\r\nYeah, some of our repository and filesystem statuses (and a few other pieces of data) are initialized via a `OnceCell` which will block other threads.\r\n\r\nI wonder if the correct thing to do there would be to separate those out into their own timings units (though I'm not sure if that's an easy change to make).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
