    "created_at": "2022-02-07T18:55:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-07T18:55:54Z",
    "body": "Aha! I figured out what was causing this. I had a share drive in my `$HOME` directory which was mounted, but unreachable. This was causing `ls` to take approximately the same time to run.\r\n\r\n> Yeah, some of our repository and filesystem statuses (and a few other pieces of data) are initialized via a OnceCell which will block other threads.\r\n\r\nThis seems to line up with what I was seeing. What's curious in the case of Starship however was that this lag occurred no matter what directory I was in. As long as there is latency to stat `$HOME`, Starship sees the same latency. Not sure if there's really a \"fix\" here, but at least maybe output a warning when that operation takes a long time?\r\n\r\n> I wonder if the correct thing to do there would be to separate those out into their own timings units (though I'm not sure if that's an easy change to make).\r\n\r\nThis would be good as well, if possible.",
